 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Vice President JD Vance takes questions from reporters during a briefing at the White House today. Photo: Kevin Dietsch/Getty Images 🎤 Vice President JD Vance today led the White House's first press briefing since July. Asked about stubborn pump pain straining Americans, Vance blamed Iranian strikes and said: "I'm not going to make a promise about when it's going to return to $3." Watch the briefing . 🤗 Nvidia announced it'll acquire open-source AI platform Hugging Face for $12.93 billion, just a month after Hugging Face was hacked by rogue OpenAI models, Axios' Dan Primack and Madison Mills report . 📺 Fox News said in a surprise announcement that longtime Fox Business host Maria Bartiromo is leaving the network. One of the network's most high-profile hosts, Bartiromo has developed a strong rapport with the president. More from Axios' Sara Fischer . 🛋️ Southwest Airlines is aiming to launch its first lounge network next year. Construction is underway on the first four lounges, coming to Baltimore, Austin, Honolulu and Nashville. Read the announcement . Gloria Steinem speaks at a rally outside the United Nations in New York in 1978. Photo: Bettye Lane/Photo Researchers History/Getty Images 🕯️ Gloria Steinem, the journalist, activist and organizer who became the most recognizable face of the U.S. women's movement, died at 92 at her home in New York City.

 Steinem co-founded Ms. magazine, bringing feminist arguments about work, sex, politics, family and reproductive rights to a mass audience, Axios' Andrew Pantazi reports . 
 
