 4. ✈️ 1 for the skies: Gateside goodbyes 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Travelers hug each other in the departure terminal at LAX last year. Photo: Apu Gomes/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Some airports are now allowing gateside sendoffs and reunions under a new TSA plan.

 Gateside passes will allow non-travelers to use PreCheck lanes to meet a friend or conduct business during a layover, shop or eat beyond security, or welcome loved ones, Axios Salt Lake City's Erin Alberty reports . 🧳 Applications opened this week for "Gateside by TSA PreCheck" access at 13 airports.

 The agency says the new offering will bring back "the moments that once defined air travel" — the kind that made Rachel get off the plane in the series finale of "Friends." How to apply ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
